COMMON STRING PATTERNS & TECHNIQUES
===============================================================================

1. TWO POINTER TECHNIQUE:
------------------------
Use for: Palindrome check, reverse string, remove duplicates

Template:
int left = 0, right = str.length() - 1;
while(left < right) {
    // Process characters at left and right
    left++;
    right--;
}

2. SLIDING WINDOW:
-----------------
Use for: Substring problems, character frequency

Template:
int left = 0;
for(int right = 0; right < str.length(); right++) {
    // Expand window by including str.charAt(right)
    
    while(/* window is invalid */) {
        // Shrink window from left
        left++;
    }
    
    // Update result with current valid window
}

3. FREQUENCY MAP:
----------------
Use for: Anagrams, character counting, duplicates

Template:
Map<Character, Integer> freq = new HashMap<>();
for(char c : str.toCharArray()) {
    freq.put(c, freq.getOrDefault(c, 0) + 1);
}

4. STRING BUILDER PATTERN:
-------------------------
Use for: String construction, reverse operations

Template:
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
// Build string efficiently
return sb.toString();

